# Personal rules (local, never committed)
# Copy to ~/.config/nousfx/local.md and edit. Sync appends this file last.
# Local files hold only what is personal; shared rules go in the harness (sync warns on repeats).
# This file goes to every tool, so keep it tool-neutral: no names that only one tool has.
# Sync warns when it finds one. Rules for one tool go in local.claude.md or local.agy.md
# in the same folder.

# How to explain things to me
- <your preferences for answer style, for example: lead with the answer, then short bullets>

# Tickets
# (The branch prefix is a setting, not a rule: it goes in local.toml, see local.toml.example.)
- Tracker: <your tracker and project key>.

# Docs voice
- <for example: write READMEs in first person>
